# Azure Virtual Machine Scale Set (VMSS) with Autoscaling

## Overview
Here's how to deploy a **VMSS** with lateral (horizontal) scaling configured for **min: 2** and **max: 5** instances.

---

## Option 1: Azure Portal

### Step 1: Create VMSS
```
Azure Portal → Virtual Machine Scale Sets → + Create
```

### Step 2: Basic Configuration
| Setting | Value |
|---------|-------|
| Subscription | Your subscription |
| Resource Group | rg-vmss-demo |
| Name | vmss-demo |
| Region | East US |
| Availability Zone | 1, 2, 3 |
| Orchestration Mode | Uniform |

### Step 3: Scaling Configuration
```
Scaling Tab:
├── Initial instance count: 2
├── Scaling Policy: Custom
├── Minimum instances: 2
└── Maximum instances: 5
```

---

## Option 2: Azure CLI

```bash
# Create Resource Group
az group create \
  --name rg-vmss-demo \
  --location eastus

# Create VMSS
az vmss create \
  --resource-group rg-vmss-demo \
  --name vmss-demo \
  --image Ubuntu2204 \
  --vm-sku Standard_B2s \
  --instance-count 2 \
  --admin-username azureuser \
  --generate-ssh-keys \
  --upgrade-policy-mode automatic

# Configure Autoscale Settings
az monitor autoscale create \
  --resource-group rg-vmss-demo \
  --resource vmss-demo \
  --resource-type Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachineScaleSets \
  --name autoscale-vmss \
  --min-count 2 \
  --max-count 5 \
  --count 2
```

### Add Scale-Out Rule (CPU > 70%)
```bash
az monitor autoscale rule create \
  --resource-group rg-vmss-demo \
  --autoscale-name autoscale-vmss \
  --condition "Percentage CPU > 70 avg 5m" \
  --scale out 1 \
  --cooldown 5
```

### Add Scale-In Rule (CPU < 30%)
```bash
az monitor autoscale rule create \
  --resource-group rg-vmss-demo \
  --autoscale-name autoscale-vmss \
  --condition "Percentage CPU < 30 avg 5m" \
  --scale in 1 \
  --cooldown 5
```

---

## Option 3: ARM Template / Bicep

```bicep
// vmss-deploy.bicep

param location string = resourceGroup().location
param vmssName string = 'vmss-demo'
param adminUsername string = 'azureuser'

@secure()
param adminPassword string

// VMSS Resource
resource vmss 'Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachineScaleSets@2023-03-01' = {
  name: vmssName
  location: location
  sku: {
    name: 'Standard_B2s'
    tier: 'Standard'
    capacity: 2  // Initial capacity
  }
  properties: {
    overprovision: true
    upgradePolicy: {
      mode: 'Automatic'
    }
    virtualMachineProfile: {
      osProfile: {
        computerNamePrefix: 'vmss'
        adminUsername: adminUsername
        adminPassword: adminPassword
      }
      storageProfile: {
        imageReference: {
          publisher: 'Canonical'
          offer: '0001-com-ubuntu-server-jammy'
          sku: '22_04-lts'
          version: 'latest'
        }
        osDisk: {
          createOption: 'FromImage'
          managedDisk: {
            storageAccountType: 'Premium_LRS'
          }
        }
      }
      networkProfile: {
        networkInterfaceConfigurations: [
          {
            name: 'vmss-nic'
            properties: {
              primary: true
              ipConfigurations: [
                {
                  name: 'vmss-ipconfig'
                  properties: {
                    subnet: {
                      id: subnet.id
                    }
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}

// Autoscale Settings
resource autoscale 'Microsoft.Insights/autoscalesettings@2022-10-01' = {
  name: 'autoscale-${vmssName}'
  location: location
  properties: {
    enabled: true
    targetResourceUri: vmss.id
    profiles: [
      {
        name: 'Auto Scale Profile'
        capacity: {
          minimum: '2'    // ✅ Minimum 2 machines
          maximum: '5'    // ✅ Maximum 5 machines
          default: '2'
        }
        rules: [
          // Scale OUT Rule
          {
            metricTrigger: {
              metricName: 'Percentage CPU'
              metricResourceUri: vmss.id
              timeGrain: 'PT1M'
              statistic: 'Average'
              timeWindow: 'PT5M'
              timeAggregation: 'Average'
              operator: 'GreaterThan'
              threshold: 70
            }
            scaleAction: {
              direction: 'Increase'
              type: 'ChangeCount'
              value: '1'
              cooldown: 'PT5M'
            }
          }
          // Scale IN Rule
          {
            metricTrigger: {
              metricName: 'Percentage CPU'
              metricResourceUri: vmss.id
              timeGrain: 'PT1M'
              statistic: 'Average'
              timeWindow: 'PT5M'
              timeAggregation: 'Average'
              operator: 'LessThan'
              threshold: 30
            }
            scaleAction: {
              direction: 'Decrease'
              type: 'ChangeCount'
              value: '1'
              cooldown: 'PT5M'
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

